Changelog: 24-11-2026 14:52:14

Release 2.0.0.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 12:57:36

Fixed. bc250-cu-bisect.sh measured a GPU load of 0% on systems whose awk is mawk, as on Debian and Ubuntu. mawk wrote
large engine times as 5e+09, which bash can't count with. The script now writes them as whole numbers. Bazzite's awk
is gawk, which wasn't affected. The load test failed in the local CI's Debian container for this reason.

Fixed. The load reading was also wrong at random where the locale writes numbers with a decimal comma, as nl_NL does.
The script's timer then read only the microseconds. It now reads the time with a point or a comma. The load test also
runs in such a locale where one is installed.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 12:21:30

Breaking. The app is now called BC-250 CU Unlock, before BC-250 CU Tools. The app key compute, its folder and file names
stay. The bottom row no longer has the label Other actions, and its pills start at the left. Show details and Show
advanced are now the pills Details and Advanced at the right end of that row. Under the name they say Show or Hide.
The window always opens 900 pixels wide, also when it was wider before. It fits its height to the page once it shows,
so a first window no longer cuts half of the page off. The tooltips are rounded boxes on the window's dark background,
as in the suite's other apps. The wiki's picture of the window shows the new row.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 04:05:33

Fixed. While a script runs, the current step's row says Running, in orange, instead of Do this now. The wiki's picture
of the window shows the step rows.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 03:54:56

Fixed. Install no longer writes the masks to the GPU while the desktop runs, because that can freeze the board.
bc250-cu-unlock.sh --install now only saves the masks and turns on the boot service. The unlock turns on at the next
restart, before the desktop starts. Step 4 then says to restart, and its Restart pill asks first.

Added. The four steps are rows at the top of the window. Each row says Done, Do this now, Stopped or Later, and what
came out of the step. The current step's row says the one thing to do, with its pill on the row. The other pills sit
at the bottom under Other actions. When everything is done, a green bar over the steps says that you're finished.
Step 4 is now called Choose and install. Active now shows the CUs the boot service applied at this boot.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 03:07:27

Fixed. The CU test measured a GPU load of 0% on the BC-250, because the kernel can't fill gpu_busy_percent there. Every
result then said "GPU load only reached 0%", and the idle check before a write could never see a busy GPU. Where that
file can't be read, the script now adds up each program's gfx and compute time from /proc/<pid>/fdinfo, as Board Test
does. On the board it read 0% at idle and 98% under memtest_vulkan.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 00:46:40

Fixed. The baseline check stopped a one-boot test after its safety check: in the same boot the registers held the
script's own writes, not the chip's, and the check refused the board's own masks. It now runs only before the first
attempt of a boot. A new file, umr-written, records the boot whose registers the script wrote, and --reset keeps it.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 00:38:43

Added. The window says the one thing to do now, in a line under the step's heading, and the pill it names has an accent
border. While a script runs, an orange turning symbol beside the pills says what runs and for how long. The window is
more compact: the hint and what comes next sit beside the pills, Show details and Show advanced sit at the right end of
the legend, and the map's cells are lower. It never opens higher than the screen, an older saved size included, and its
page scrolls when needed. Refresh is the suite's small round symbol beside the info symbol, a copy of core's
RefreshButton, not a framed button.

Fixed. During a test the window stayed on the step it started from, for example Scan during the whole safety check,
without the live line. It now reads the results again at every attempt and moves to the step that runs. Step 1 no
longer says "with the restarts" when the test runs in one boot.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 00:00:03

Fixed. The wiki chapter explains the CU counts in one highlighted box near its top, "24, 32 or 40 CUs, and the counts
in between". It holds that the 24 stock CUs differ per board, why only 24, 32 and 40 CUs help, the example masks,
and the counts in between, such as 34, 36 and 38 CUs. The step-by-step part and How it works point to it. The
window's link Why uneven CUs don't help now leads to the box.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 23:55:44

Fixed. The wiki chapter opens with a box that says the 24 stock CUs differ per board. Which 2 WGPs per shader
array a chip has switched off differs per chip, so the stock masks differ too. The chapter assumed
0x07,0x07,0x07,0x07 on every board before. The masks in its first table are now marked as examples.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 23:52:38

Added. The board doesn't go to sleep while a test runs. Each test run of the script holds the standard sleep block of
systemd-inhibit, with the reason "A CU test is running", and the block ends with the run. The scan and the report
don't block sleep.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 23:50:27

Added. When a test ends, the window shows a desktop notification that stays until you click it. It says that the
test is done, with the WGPs that fail and the highest even level, or that it stopped, or how the combined test went.
Stop and Pause send none. The notification goes through notify-send, as Board Test's do.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 23:47:04

Added. The map has a Mask column: each row's mask as a hex value, with the same bits under it. Step 1 names the
board's own masks in one line. Same boot is on by default, so a test runs every attempt in one boot, asks for the
password once and needs no one by the board. After the safety check passes, the WGP test starts by itself. The
window keeps one terminal for all its script runs, so sudo asks once. Turn Same boot off to test a failing WGP again
with a restart per attempt. The autostart entry opens the same window and scripts that started the test, also from
a checkout.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 23:10:48

Added. Step 4 of the window shows the uneven CU counts between the highest even level and all healthy WGPs, for
example 34, 36 and 38 CUs, with the WGPs per row. They are status boxes for comparison with other tools and can't be
applied. A link beside them leads to the wiki's explanation of why uneven CUs don't help.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 22:59:57

Fixed. bc250-cu-bisect.sh refuses a baseline that switches off a WGP the chip runs, and names that WGP and the
board's own masks. The chip marks its switched-off WGPs in CC_GC_SHADER_ARRAY_CONFIG, and they differ per board. On
a board with 0x07,0x07,0x07,0x0b, the baseline 0x07,0x07,0x07,0x07 turned a working WGP off and a switched-off one
on. Its control then reset the GPU. The window's Baseline field is gone, with its choices Stock, 24 CUs, Unlocked,
40 CUs and Custom.... The test always starts from the board's own masks. The wiki said that stock is
0x07,0x07,0x07,0x07 on every board. That was wrong, and the chapter now says the stock masks differ per board.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 22:35:20

Added. bc250-cu-bisect.sh has a test option for the unlock method itself, --writes. It writes only the registers you
name, from cc, spi and rlc. Without it, the script writes all three, as before. The script now also shows the live
value of RLC_PG_ALWAYS_ON_WGP_MASK beside the masks and CC. A result written with --writes says which registers in
its note.

Changelog: 23-11-2026 22:00:34

Added. The window runs the CU test itself, in four steps, and no terminal opens anymore. Step 1 scans the board.
Step 2 runs the safety check, which is the control. Step 3 tests each locked WGP. In step 4 you choose 24, 32 or 40
CUs, and the window runs the combined test and installs the unlock. A map shows each WGP's state in words and color.
The window asks once before the test. It then restarts the board by itself after each attempt, with a countdown and
Pause. An autostart entry, ~/.config/autostart/bc250-cu-tools-resume.desktop, opens it again after each login. When
the safety check fails, the window stops and says that the unlock method breaks on this board. Load per attempt,
Rounds per item, Baseline, Same boot and No watch are under Show advanced. Control only, Unattended and Auto resume
are gone from the window. The safety check and the combined test do what Control only did. The script keeps
--control-only and --auto. The window no longer installs bc250-cu-bisect-auto.service. Preview a mask and Re-check
are gone, and the round refresh symbol reads the results again. The uninstall removes the autostart entry.
bc250-cu-bisect.sh has two new options. --scan reads the live masks and what a run needs, and writes no register.
--only ITEM runs the attempts of one item only. With BC250_GUI=1 the script prints lines for the window and asks its
questions as whole lines. Without it, the script works as before. The "Changes the board" text in the portal and the
wiki chapter says how the window restarts the board now.

